Let <math>x</math> and <math>y</math> be random variables that are independently and uniformly distributed in the interval <math>(0,1).</math> Note that <cmath>P(x+y\leq 1)=\frac{\frac12\cdot1^2}{1^2}=\frac12,</cmath> as shown below:
<asy>
/* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */
size(200); 

real xMin = -0.25;
real xMax = 1.25;
real yMin = -0.25;
real yMax = 1.25;

